# Source intervals are independently selected after reading the whole relevant entries/sections.
source_defs={
'рукав':(D2,56016,56033,'РУКАВ, complete four senses and both idioms','Clothing covering arm/part of arm; the listed idioms ALSO have diligent/careless readings; river branch is sense2, tube/duct sense3, long passage/device sense4. The listing does not force a figurative reading of every finite «засучил рукава». The original PNG was visually read in initial review; this session reread the complete current saved text.'),
'закатать':(D1,47636,47655,'ЗАКАТАТЬ, complete six senses','Sense2 explicitly «Подвернуть, засучить. Закатать рукава, штаны»; other senses wrap by rolling, flatten, imprison, tire by riding, seal jars. This is positive primary support for literal sleeve-rolling, not an intuition-only objection.'),
'оголить':(D2,5229,5243,'ОГОЛИТЬ, complete four senses','Exact literal example «Засучив рукава, оголил руки до локтей». Other senses remove leaves, expose covering, weaken a position. This directly refutes author assertion that sleeve-rolling cannot name clothing parts in the current option0.'),
'надеть':(D1,85109,85121,'НАДЕТЬ, complete three senses','Sense1 что на кого-что, examples шубу на ребёнка, чехол на кресло, на дверь цепочку; sense2 что, clothe oneself, exact «Надеть пальто»; sense3 thread/impale a bead/bait. Distinguishes current options1/3 while supplying the old correct-note extra fact lost in revision.'),
'одеть':(D2,5562,5582,'ОДЕТЬ, complete five senses','Sense1 clothe, exact малыш/больной/кукла; sense2 supply clothes; senses3–5 cover/envelop, face a surface, cover with blanket. Current other-person option0 is grammatical. The blanket statement that одеть always requires a person must be read only within the stated clothing context.'),
'обуть':(D2,3689,3698,'ОБУТЬ, complete two senses','Put footwear on someone or on feet (валенки/туфли), figuratively fit tyres; supply footwear. Read to distinguish this from the adjacent reflexive entry actually needed for current option2.'),
'обуться':(D2,3699,3705,'ОБУТЬСЯ, complete two senses','Sense1 put footwear on one’s own feet, sense2 supply oneself with footwear. Supports current grammatical continuation «он должен обуться», but neither meaning specifies a coat.'),
'смелый':(D2,67373,67391,'СМЕЛЫЙ, complete four senses','Sense1 not yielding to fear/dangers: explicit храбрый, отважный; sense2 resolute/novel-seeking; sense3 topical/sharp content; sense4 beyond convention/immodest. Restricted prompt chooses sense1 and correct note adds verified separate sense2.'),
'храбрый':(D2,105195,105201,'ХРАБРЫЙ, complete entry','Definition отважный, смелый, exact example «Храбрый боец». Also actions/manifestations of courage and negative idiom не из храброго десятка. The exact replacement is independently confirmed, not inherited from synonym metadata.'),
'робкий':(D2,55049,55056,'РОБКИЙ, complete entry','Несмелый, боязливый; examples character/child and manifestations; «не робкого десятка» explicitly means brave. Supports note1 including its extra idiom information, not just exclusion of the answer.'),
'скрытный':(D2,65554,65566,'СКРЫТНЫЙ, complete both senses and adverb','Sense1 hides thoughts/feelings/intentions (person); sense2 undetected/hidden from others and adverb action examples. Current brave option names a person, so sense1 is appropriate here, unlike the previous spustya action-note defect.'),
'медлительный':(D1,78434,78443,'МЕДЛИТЕЛЬНЫЙ, complete both senses','Acting/moving without haste, slowly; measured/calm/unhurried, examples motions/speech. Current brave option modifies a person; tempo does not imply fearlessness.'),
'зарубить':(D1,50350,50361,'ЗАРУБИТЬ, complete four senses','Sense1 kill with chopping weapon and bear example; sense2 notch log/tree; sense3 take note/remember forever with future/statement/words-in-memory examples; sense4 mining cut. The exact phrase «на носу» is ABSENT from the complete article, confirmed visually on PDF204. Cannot silently attribute that phrase to these examples.'),
'нос':(D1,97269,97295,'НОС, complete six senses','Face organ, beak, front of vehicle, toe of shoe, spout, place-name component; the exact «зарубить на носу» is absent from this article too. This bounded cross-check is evidence of the supplied-locator gap, not a claim that no primary source anywhere contains the idiom.'),
'деепричастие':(D1,34978,34990,'ДЕЕПРИЧАСТИЕ, full definition/bullet/derived form','Explicitly an invariant FORM OF A VERB, combining verb/adverb properties and additional action. Questions include что делая/сделав, category list вид/переходность/время, adverbial meaning. Visual PDF142 resolves examples missing from text and confirms the source’s exact tense wording. That wording is an attribution to this source, not an invented universal grammar rule.'),
'предлог':(D2,33721,33729,'ПРЕДЛОГ (grammatical homonym), complete entry','Service part of speech expressing connection of noun/pronoun/numeral with other words; simple/compound distinction. This independently supplies the non-key note3 relation claim omitted by author’s sole gerund-definition locator.'),
'частиречи-введение':(G,56,102,'Сичинава, full introduction §1','Morphological/syntactic/semantic criteria can yield different inventories. Usual ten-class inventory includes verb/adverb/preposition and not participle/gerund; other classifications split classes. Essential qualification for a question unconditionally asking which part of speech a gerund is.'),
'частиречи-служебные':(G,250,300,'Сичинава §3.1, relevant complete contrast before interjections discussion','Content classes name situations/participants and are sentence members; service classes connect/express auxiliary meanings, prepositions have government. Confirms why smiling additional action is not a linking preposition.'),
'причастие-деепричастие':(G,757,792,'Сичинава §5.2 introduction and COMPLETE §5.2.1','Participles often, gerunds sometimes treated as separate POS; adjective-declining agreeing participles vs invariant gerunds differ from finite verbs. Author discusses lexical/traditional objections and hybrid-class treatment. Full section crosses PDF20–21 (printed28–29); author page21-only citation misses the core agreement/declension sentence on PDF20.'),
'тире10':(R,8269,8287,'Лопатин2006 complete §10 and complete note','Dash in missing-copula nominative noun subject/predicate. May be absent under written logical emphasis on predicate; obligatory in juxtaposition or ambiguity. All examples and exceptions read and PDF208 visually inspected, including which words have bold emphasis.'),
'запятая112':(R,11339,11454,'Лопатин2006 complete §112 including exceptions','Compound clause comma basic rule, relations/examples, repeated-ли note and all five no-comma conditions. Current note uses its general clause-separation function; none applies to the single Moscow clause. Starts PDF282 (printed280), not author PDF283.'),
'точкасзапятой128':(R,11919,11963,'Лопатин2006 COMPLETE §128 and note','Extended clauses can be separated by semicolon, preferred for internal comma structure; note includes semantic independence and compound blocks. Current simple Moscow sentence lacks multiple predicative parts. Section starts PDF296, continues297 (printed294–295).'),
'двоеточие129':(R,11964,12076,'Лопатин2006 COMPLETE §129 including all four notes','Explanatory, causal, content clauses; substitution tests; perception comma option, dash alternatives, title-like nominal constructions and mandatory colon before subordinate explanation. Current ordinary sentence isn’t a title or a multi-clause relation. Section spans PDF297–300; the author page300/lines11964–11983 pairing is mismatched, and cited lines alone omit causal condition11993ff.')}
